{"id": "EUVD-2026-59259", "enisaUuid": "cc070b05-d76f-3d10-8517-28cc856fb483", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/xe/pf: Don't attempt to process FAST_REQ or EVENT relays\n\nCurrently defined VF/PF relay actions use regular REQUEST messages\nonly and the PF shouldn't attempt to handle FAST_REQUEST nor EVENT\nmessages as this would result in breaking the VFPF ABI protocol\nand also might trigger an assert on the PF side.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 1714d360fc5ae2e0886a69e979095d9c7ff3568a)", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:56:00", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T18:55:20", "baseScore": 8.4, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:N/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/499be4b5d64209e9f18c9442f9fbeef7155ae900", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/adc7dda728ca3e340a413e3bbc10cf159e1866a4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a4208d8032abd7f591581994f31e23b80b8fe659", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ed8b0d731892c68b41ecbd27c952af284816dec1"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-72360", "GHSA-g429-9jp7-485v"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1daefc9a-27c1-3412-a1ef-3668f7344200", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.11"}, {"id": "3f9dd9af-e86f-3e8c-b72b-8ba60f038b56", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "61cedc18-a1be-3271-aeb6-22347f24fcf4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.40"}, {"id": "7d11bd37-6836-3925-9bd7-18c0daab6810", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "98e62805921cebcd2fcac3692037ca2ebef63b4a <499be4b5d64209e9f18c9442f9fbeef7155ae900"}, {"id": "82e9c011-7e4c-3cdf-98fe-e066f217c848", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "98e62805921cebcd2fcac3692037ca2ebef63b4a <ed8b0d731892c68b41ecbd27c952af28